# Project review rules

The verify and UI review agents cite these headings, next to the skill's own `references/review-rules.md`. Write rules a reviewer can check in the diff or the browser, each with the reason. Mark the ones that block a ship with (BLOCKING).

## Example: users only see the new UI (BLOCKING)
- Non-admins never reach `/legacy/*`; they are redirected to the `/app/*` equivalent. Signed-out visitors go to `/login`.
- Why: the legacy pages skip the new permission checks.

## Example: naming
- User-facing text says "Workspace", never the old name "Project".
